@REQ-OSA-11 @REQ-OSA-12 @REQ-OSA-13 @REQ-OSA-14 @REQ-OSA-15 @REQ-OSA-29 @NFR-OSA-2
Feature: spec-rails installer for OpenSpec projects
  As a team running OpenSpec
  We want "spec-rails" to wire itself into an existing openspec/ project
  So that Spec-Rails gates, hooks and CI are added without disturbing OpenSpec.

  @REQ-OSA-11 @REQ-OSA-12 @REQ-OSA-29
  Scenario: Fresh install
    Given a repo initialized with "openspec init" and OpenSpec >= 1.15.0
    When the installer runs
    Then "openspec/schemas/spec-rails/schema.yaml" exists
    And "openspec/config.yaml" has "schema: spec-rails"
    And the pre-commit config, CI workflow, mutation templates, branch-protection hook, skill and agent rules are present
    And ".gitignore" contains ".worktrees/"

  @REQ-OSA-13
  Scenario: Idempotent re-run
    Given a completed install
    When the installer runs again
    Then no file changes
    And the exit code is 0

  @REQ-OSA-11
  Scenario: Missing prerequisite
    Given a directory without "openspec/"
    When the installer runs
    Then it exits non-zero with a message
    And nothing is written

  @REQ-OSA-11
  Scenario: Old or absent OpenSpec CLI
    Given "openspec" is missing from PATH or reports a version below 1.15.0
    When the installer runs
    Then it exits non-zero naming the required version
    And nothing is written

  @REQ-OSA-14
  Scenario: Config preservation
    Given "openspec/config.yaml" with "context" and "rules" keys
    When the installer runs
    Then those keys are unchanged
    And "schema: spec-rails" is set

  @REQ-OSA-14
  Scenario: Existing pre-commit config is kept
    Given a user ".pre-commit-config.yaml"
    When the installer runs
    Then that file is byte-identical afterwards

  Scenario: Another schema already set
    Given "openspec/config.yaml" with "schema: spec-driven"
    When the installer runs
    Then "schema: spec-rails" is set
    And the previous value "spec-driven" is printed

  Scenario: No config.yaml
    Given "openspec/" without "config.yaml"
    When the installer runs
    Then "openspec/config.yaml" is created containing only "schema: spec-rails"

  Scenario: Target is not a git repository
    Given an OpenSpec project that is not a git repository
    When the installer runs
    Then hooks are skipped with a warning
    And schema and config wiring still occur
    And the exit code is 0

  @REQ-OSA-15
  Scenario: Rules survive "openspec update"
    Given a completed install
    Then Spec-Rails rules live outside files regenerated by "openspec update"

  @NFR-OSA-2
  Scenario: Installer latency budget
    Given an OpenSpec project with 0 active changes
    When the installer runs
    Then it completes within 5 seconds excluding OpenSpec startup
